.TH BACKGROUND 2 2000-1月 "KO.background" "KO.background"
.SH NAME
KO.background \- create kegg background model
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fIKO.background(\fBgenes\fR as any, 
\fBmaps\fR as any, 
\fBsize\fR as integer = -1, 
\fBgenomeName\fR as string = "unknown", 
\fBid_map\fR as any = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
\fBmultiple_omics\fR as boolean = FALSE, 
\fBterm_db\fR as string = "unknown", 
\fBinstance_map\fR as <generic> dataframe = \fB<NULL>\fR, 
[\fB<Environment>\fR]);\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
create kegg background model
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fBgenes\fB \fR\- a set of molecules with the kegg orthology/compound id mapping. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmaps\fB \fR\- the kegg maps model. 
.PP
.PP
\fBsize\fB \fR\- the background gene size, default -1 or zero means auto calculation.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBgenomeName\fB \fR\- the genome name that tagged with this background model.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBid_map\fB \fR\- 
 an optional id mapping data for the gene id, the ko id and the gene name, it could be
 a \fBlist\fR object or a \fBdataframe\fR object. Default \fBNULL\fR means no extra id mapping.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBmultiple_omics\fB \fR\- 
 creates the background model for the multiple omics data analysis? Default \fBFALSE\fR.
. 
.PP
.PP
\fBterm_db\fB \fR\- the database label of the term that will be written into the result model. Default \fBunknown\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBinstance_map\fB \fR\- the compound instance map that is used for the metabolism enrichment analysis. Default \fBNULL\fR.. 
.PP
.PP
\fBenv\fB \fR\- the R# runtime environment.. 
.PP
.SH VALUE
.PP
a [Background](cref:T:SMRUCC.genomics.Analysis.HTS.GSEA.Background) model that is created from the given KO id mapping.
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
background
.SH FILES
.PP
gseakit.dll
.PP
